<title>SPAIN: BT doesn't see problems with EU deal approval.</title>
<headline>BT doesn't see problems with EU deal approval.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of British Telecommunications Plc, Iain Vallance, said on Friday that he did not expect &quot;significant problems&quot; with the European Union for its and MCI's deal with Telefonica.</p>
<p>When asked if the new deal had to be approved by the EU Commission, Vallance told journalists in Madrid, &quot;This would have to be approved by the EC but we had preliminary talks this morning with the Commission and I don't expect significant problems in this deal, but we have to be careful&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
